# The guard files: what makes CI and review enforce the standards. A change here can weaken a check unseen, so it
# needs the maintainer's review (CONTRIBUTING, "Files that need the maintainer's review"). Agent instructions and
# hooks also run on a maintainer's machine when they work on a branch; workflows and scripts run with the repository's
# rights. The core and the database are not listed: they change daily and CI's checks and tests cover them.
/.github/workflows/                  @ziffr
/.github/scripts/                    @ziffr
/.github/CODEOWNERS                  @ziffr
/.github/calculation-paths.txt       @ziffr
/scripts/                            @ziffr
/knip.jsonc                          @ziffr
/.jscpd.json                         @ziffr
/eslint.code-health.mjs              @ziffr
/packages/core/stryker.config.mjs    @ziffr
/.vale.ini                           @ziffr
/.vale/                              @ziffr
/AGENTS.md                           @ziffr
/CLAUDE.md                           @ziffr
/.claude/                            @ziffr
/CONTRIBUTING.md                     @ziffr
/LICENSE                             @ziffr
/NOTICE                              @ziffr
/CLA.md                              @ziffr
